# Identity feeds authorization

## Package recommendation

When both plugins are installed: Authentication establishes the request identity; Authorization uses that identity in policies and authorize calls. Keep the boundary sharp.

## Required behavior

- Configure middleware order so identity is available before authorization checks that need it.
- Login/session/token success ≠ permission; still authorize resource actions.
- Reuse one identity source — do not maintain parallel “current user” hacks.
- Test matrices: anonymous, authenticated-but-forbidden, authenticated-and-allowed.

## Anti-patterns

- Duplicating role tables in both login and every policy inconsistently
- Skipping Authorization because Authentication middleware already ran
